<!--
    Workspaces M1 (#54, ADR-001): the per-leaf tab strip is now the REAL MUX
    TabView (Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls.TabView), the same control the classic
    per-window tab row uses (see TabRowControl.xaml). It replaces the old
    re-skinned WUX ListView whose classic-TabViewItem chrome — rounded top,
    bottom flare/chamfer, inter-tab separators, hover highlight — was hand-built
    as a model projection (the "RECONCILE BEFORE UPSTREAM PR" brush block,
    deleted). Native TabViewItem chrome / icon / tooltip now render that look.

    The TabView is driven by WorkspaceModel through MANUAL TabView.TabItems()
    projection in TabStripView.cpp (NOT TabItemsSource binding). Selection is a
    one-way projection of the model (the page pushes SelectedItem from the
    ActiveTabChanged diff; a user SelectionChanged is an intent only,
    reentrancy-guarded).

    Drag is FULLY on (Workspaces M6a + M6b, #54): all three flags are TRUE.
    CanReorderTabs="True" enables the WITHIN-leaf reorder (M6a) — MUX mutates
    TabItems internally during the drag; TabStripView captures the from/to off
    TabItemsChanged and raises a MoveTabRequested intent on TabDragCompleted, so the
    page dispatches moveTab and the TabMoved diff re-projects (no write-back).
    CanDragTabs="True" + AllowDropTabs="True" enable the CROSS-leaf (inter-control)
    move (M6b): the source strip stuffs the dragged VM's Id + our PID into the
    DataPackage on TabDragStarting; a sibling strip accepts the Move on
    TabStripDragOver (PID-guarded) and, on TabStripDrop, hit-tests the drop index
    and raises the SAME MoveTabRequested intent with ITS OWN LeafId as the
    destination. AllowDropTabs="True" arms the tear-out dispatcher, so the
    matching TabDroppedOutside handler MUST be wired (it is — an INERT no-op,
    the M8 boundary) or a drag-out crashes Windows.UI.Xaml.dll (0xc000027b —
    drag-out of a draggable TabView with no handler). The four cross-leaf
    handlers (TabDragStarting / TabStripDragOver / TabStripDrop /
    TabDroppedOutside) are wired in the ctor.

    IsAddTabButtonVisible is false in M1: the native "+" → new-tab-in-this-leaf
    wiring is a SHOULD that we DEFER (see the .cpp). The mux namespace + the
    Background="TabViewBackground" mirror TabRowControl.xaml.
-->
<UserControl x:Class="TerminalApp.TabStripView"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:local="using:TerminalApp"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             xmlns:mux="using:Microsoft.UI.Xaml.Controls"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <mux:TabView x:Name="TabView"
                 Background="{ThemeResource TabViewBackground}"
                 AllowDropTabs="True"
                 CanDragTabs="True"
                 CanReorderTabs="True"
                 IsAddTabButtonVisible="False"
                 TabWidthMode="SizeToContent" />

</UserControl>
